WaxHive is a modified version of GNOME Music.
Upstream: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gnome-music
WaxHive: https://github.com/Morph-777/WaxHive

GNOME Music copyright notices, contributor credits, license text, and the
GStreamer exception are retained. The original authors' credits are available
in the application's About dialog and throughout the source and Git history.
The GNOME Music icon is retained with its existing license.

WaxHive changes by Morph (2026) include the album-artist desktop layout,
compact album and playback views, configurable artwork corners, persistent
panel sizing, keyboard navigation, and separate Flatpak packaging.
These changes use the same GPL-2.0-or-later license and GStreamer exception
as the application code they extend. LICENSE contains the original terms.

Third-party dependencies retain their respective licenses. Their pinned
source archives and repository revisions are listed in
io.github.Morph777.WaxHive.json and subprojects/shared-modules.
